[[2047,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The optional services relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 controls the heating circuit\nfor the seats as well as the electric rear windows and sun roof: \n\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3060\n\t\tSUN ROOF\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 , \n\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 See\n\t\tE3051\n\t\tELECTRIC REAR WINDOWS\n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 \n                                 .</strong></p>"],[2047,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The coil for relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 is energized when\nthe ignition is switched on (INT/A) by the line for fuse B10, whilst\nthe supply at the relay contact arrives from the battery, through\nthe line for maxifuse J/B2 of B5.</strong></p>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The coil of the relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J60 is energized\nwhen the ignition is switched on (INT/A) by the line for fuse F6\nof the additional fuse box B98B, while the supply at the relay contact\narrives from the battery, through the line for maxifuse J/B2 of\nB99.</strong></p>"],[2047,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>By pressing the switch on the\nseat the resistors for the heaters in the left and right seats, \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>040\nand 041, connected in parallel, are supplied, until a thermal contact\ninside the heaters disconnects the resistors when the temperature\nexceeds a certain limit.</strong></p><p>This supply passes through the heated seats\nfuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which guarantees the protection of the circuit\nand reaches the switches in the seats through connection \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>D70</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (left\nseat) and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>D71</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (right seat): the supply for the two devices\nis therefore controlled by the ignition (INT/A) and they are connected\nto earth \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When the resistors are on, an LED signals\nthe operation of the device.</p>"]]